1
00:00:13,240 --> 00:00:14,993
[tn]: Well, it's the same line we're talking now,

2
00:00:15,406 --> 00:00:17,865
[tn]: That the hindrances we were speaking about the other day.

3
00:00:19,949 --> 00:00:21,406
[tn]: They belong to the body.

4
00:00:23,110 --> 00:00:23,818
[tn]: Without...

5
00:00:25,772 --> 00:00:28,227
[tn]: They cannot arise without the body.

6
00:00:28,286 --> 00:00:31,221
[nm]: Inseparable from... Yeah.

7
00:00:31,806 --> 00:00:38,370
[tn]: And the hindrances being... Oh, [?I forgot what I had to say].

8
00:00:38,770 --> 00:00:41,326
[tn]: Weakners, a corruptions of mind, weakeners of wisdom.

9
00:00:41,338 --> 00:00:43,621
[nm]: Yeah, weakining, weakners of wisdom, and so...

10
00:00:44,665 --> 00:00:49,221
[tn]: And it's always like the first, you know, if you can abandon those...

11
00:00:50,572 --> 00:00:52,437
[tn]: I don't know if it means to destroy those.

12
00:00:53,010 --> 00:00:54,294
[nm]: Well, no.

13
00:00:54,324 --> 00:01:06,934
[nm]: Arahant fully goes beyond hindrance, whereby any... any hindrance that arises, it's not a hindrance for him, because his mind is beyond that, or above it, so they don't...

14
00:01:07,090 --> 00:01:07,743
[tn]: But they're still...

15
00:01:08,190 --> 00:01:09,856
[nm]: Well, no, it's not a hindrance then.

16
00:01:10,320 --> 00:01:12,366
[nm]: Say the same body has moods.

17
00:01:13,865 --> 00:01:16,934
[nm]: Bodily existence of the five aggregates has moods.

18
00:01:17,953 --> 00:01:21,170
[nm]: And that mood is taking you.

19
00:01:21,650 --> 00:01:22,858
[nm]: It's throwing you about.

20
00:01:23,524 --> 00:01:25,658
[nm]: Because your mind is somewhere wedged in between.

21
00:01:25,670 --> 00:01:29,216
[nm]: Weak and confused in regard to it and appropriating it as mine.

22
00:01:30,080 --> 00:01:31,772
[nm]: For an arahant, it's completely free.

23
00:01:32,067 --> 00:01:35,452
[nm]: Free from any appropriation, any conceiving, whatever else.

24
00:01:35,630 --> 00:01:39,461
[nm]: They truly remain just bodily... moods.

25
00:01:41,044 --> 00:01:58,538
[nm]: In other words, whatever arises, it won't be a hindrance. And it will never develop to the extent that it used to develop, because it used to develop because it was a hindrance, because you did take it as mine, and then revolved around it even more, and proliferated even further.

26
00:01:59,738 --> 00:02:07,098
[tn]: So, you got into that mood of whatever, ill-will, lust, and then you just... you were taken over by this.

27
00:02:07,610 --> 00:02:09,393
[nm]: Well, yeah, and then it becomes [?mine a bit / mind].

28
00:02:09,400 --> 00:02:24,265
[nm]: But like lust, for example, it takes a while, like sexual desire, for example, it takes a while before it becomes a full-on sexual desire.

29
00:02:24,580 --> 00:02:30,037
[nm]: And when I say it takes a while, I mean it takes some time of attending it wrongly,

30
00:02:31,090 --> 00:02:35,671
[nm]: Giving attention to the sound of beauty, getting wound up, getting excited, [?and so on].

31
00:02:36,096 --> 00:02:38,484
[nm]: And then, yeah, then you can be in that state perpetually.

32
00:02:40,181 --> 00:02:41,389
[nm]: Or state of ill-will.

33
00:02:41,380 --> 00:02:43,347
[nm]: But nevertheless, they take time to develop.

34
00:02:44,060 --> 00:02:51,831
[nm]: Basically, that developing means this kind of revolving, when you don't know the escape from the initial itch of sexual desire, which is purely bodily.

35
00:02:53,020 --> 00:03:00,408
[nm]: Because for as long as there is a body, for as long as there is a prostate organ, and penis, and everything else, there will be...

36
00:03:01,541 --> 00:03:04,320
[nm]: a possibility of an itch.

37
00:03:05,616 --> 00:03:06,795
[nm]: And that's all turd.

38
00:03:08,673 --> 00:03:16,762
[nm]: Obviously, the whole significance of the sexual organs, sensuality, and everything else, and the whole appropriation of that, means it's never seen just as an itch.

39
00:03:16,760 --> 00:03:17,574
[nm]: Well, sometimes.

40
00:03:17,890 --> 00:03:20,960
[nm]: But again, even when it is, it's seen as my itch.

41
00:03:21,776 --> 00:03:30,661
[nm]: And since there is nothing preventing you from stopping it, from not indulging it, people don't understand the danger of indulging it,

42
00:03:31,420 --> 00:03:31,936
[nm]: they do it.

43
00:03:33,204 --> 00:03:35,170
[nm]: Maybe not physically, but they do it mentally.

44
00:03:36,960 --> 00:03:39,347
[nm]: They nurture it, they cherish it, they entertain it.

45
00:03:41,183 --> 00:03:41,890
[tn]: You give in to it.

46
00:03:42,390 --> 00:03:43,132
[nm]: Well, yeah.

47
00:03:43,520 --> 00:03:48,298
[nm]: You might be resisting, but let's say a layman, yeah, you fully lay your plank.

48
00:03:48,635 --> 00:03:52,214
[nm]: You take on the reins, not just... you go for it.

49
00:03:53,740 --> 00:03:54,947
[nm]: But it was purely bodily.

50
00:03:55,212 --> 00:03:56,920
[nm]: And it always remains inseparable.

51
00:03:56,934 --> 00:03:58,842
[nm]: Imagine if there is no body.

52
00:03:59,658 --> 00:04:02,033
[nm]: Would you be able to experience sexual desire?

53
00:04:02,538 --> 00:04:06,682
[nm]: Imagine if there is no mouth, no tongue, would you be able to enjoy the tasty food?

54
00:04:06,854 --> 00:04:07,456
[nm]: You wouldn't.

55
00:04:07,860 --> 00:04:08,492
[nm]: You couldn't.

56
00:04:08,871 --> 00:04:10,046
[nm]: Inseparable from.

57
00:04:10,526 --> 00:04:17,877
[nm]: So, any food that you ever enjoyed, any food that you are enjoying, any food that you will enjoy, is completely bound to your tongue.

58
00:04:18,488 --> 00:04:19,052
[nm]: Literally.

59
00:04:21,945 --> 00:04:23,326
[tn]: It's completely bodily.

60
00:04:23,640 --> 00:04:26,522
[nm]: In that... Because of that, it's entirely bodily.

61
00:04:29,212 --> 00:04:32,248
[nm]: Because all of the other permutations can happen, come and go.

62
00:04:33,082 --> 00:04:35,077
[nm]: But this remains as a necessary condition.

63
00:04:35,820 --> 00:04:42,033
[nm]: Presence of a working tongue, working eyes, working ears.

64
00:04:43,928 --> 00:04:44,943
[nm]: But that's not the problem.

65
00:04:45,566 --> 00:04:52,648
[nm]: Because if eyes and what they see would be a problem, if tongue and the taste would be a problem, removing the tongue would remove the problem.

66
00:04:54,472 --> 00:04:56,132
[nm]: But none of it is the problem.

67
00:04:56,804 --> 00:04:57,785
[nm]: Your mind is not the problem.

68
00:04:57,814 --> 00:04:58,905
[nm]: Your thoughts are not the problem.

69
00:05:04,665 --> 00:05:05,473
[tn]: It's just a craving.

70
00:05:05,831 --> 00:05:07,204
[nm]: It's just a craving in regard to it.

71
00:05:07,856 --> 00:05:09,482
[tn]: The assumption that the body is one.

72
00:05:09,610 --> 00:05:10,644
[nm]: Well, it all comes out of it.

73
00:05:12,080 --> 00:05:15,431
[nm]: Mind and conceit and craving all revolve around the same thing.

74
00:05:15,907 --> 00:05:16,517
[nm]: Ignorance.

75
00:05:17,898 --> 00:05:18,589
[nm]: You conceive.

76
00:05:18,600 --> 00:05:19,583
[nm]: You take it as yours.

77
00:05:19,580 --> 00:05:20,475
[nm]: You're taking me.

78
00:05:22,273 --> 00:05:25,898
[nm]: Then you become, you know, that which chases after the counterpart.

79
00:05:27,035 --> 00:05:32,816
[nm]: So, for as long as you're identifying with your masculine body, masculine sexual organ,

80
00:05:34,033 --> 00:05:41,254
[nm]: masculine possibility of sexual pleasure, of sensual pleasure in general, you will be bound by that pleasure.

81
00:05:41,612 --> 00:05:51,406
[nm]: Even if you are restraining, even if you spend the rest of your life as a celibate restraining, if you don't sever the connection internally, you will... you remain bound, you remain in sensual domain.

82
00:05:52,410 --> 00:05:54,345
[tn]: I mean, you're just saying no, but you're not...

83
00:05:54,538 --> 00:05:57,050
[nm]: Yeah, you're not actually freeing yourself from it.

84
00:05:57,720 --> 00:06:02,905
[nm]: Saying no is the first step, but it's the first step that can only enable you to see the escaot,

85
00:06:02,913 --> 00:06:03,974
[nm]: It's not the escape itself.

86
00:06:15,840 --> 00:06:25,347
[tn]: If I step back in reflection, when I look at the body that appears, in whatever form it appears in,

87
00:06:27,204 --> 00:06:28,433
[tn]: Might be a sensation.

88
00:06:29,320 --> 00:06:31,195
[nm]: Mhmh... Well...

89
00:06:31,195 --> 00:06:32,370
[tn]: The physical breathing or the...

90
00:06:32,429 --> 00:06:35,406
[nm]: See, that's already... your body was already there beforehand.

91
00:06:36,037 --> 00:06:40,336
[nm]: Because that sensation was being possible to be manifested because the body was already there.

92
00:06:41,658 --> 00:06:42,901
[tn]: But I don't see it.

93
00:06:43,616 --> 00:06:44,560
[nm]: Because you're not mindful of it.

94
00:06:45,700 --> 00:06:57,246
[nm]: Because... And another reason why you don't see it, is because, for you, only that particular manifestation of this or that, that manifests the body, is the manifestation of the body.

95
00:06:58,825 --> 00:07:12,585
[nm]: But if you develop knowledge that actually, any of those particular manifestations are possible only because the body is already there, that thought, the body is already there, starts to stand, begins standing for that which is the body in your experience.

96
00:07:13,050 --> 00:07:15,115
[nm]: In other words, that is your body and your experience.

97
00:07:15,292 --> 00:07:16,096
[nm]: There is no in-between.

98
00:07:16,151 --> 00:07:17,752
[tn]: The thought that the body is already there.

99
00:07:17,936 --> 00:07:18,210
[nm]: Yeah.

100
00:07:19,230 --> 00:07:26,273
[nm]: Because, again, would you be able to think anything about the body, if that body is not standing there?

101
00:07:27,178 --> 00:07:29,658
[tn]: But you can't know it any other way.

102
00:07:29,690 --> 00:07:30,922
[nm]: Well, exactly.

103
00:07:31,031 --> 00:07:33,056
[nm]: You can't access that through the senses.

104
00:07:33,444 --> 00:07:38,193
[nm]: Sensations, sights, sensations of touch, sights, sounds, smell, that's all sensual.

105
00:07:38,580 --> 00:07:39,818
[nm]: That all comes through senses.

106
00:07:40,349 --> 00:07:42,109
[nm]: And that's usually the criteria for

107
00:07:43,128 --> 00:07:47,305
[nm]: what exists, put it in [?vertical, but] exists much more than that.

108
00:07:48,345 --> 00:08:00,694
[nm]: So, but when you know that all those things are possible only because the body is already there, and that body is already there, because you're thinking it, you realize, ah, that's how the mind comes first, because this all precedes it.

109
00:08:01,073 --> 00:08:04,202
[nm]: That thought of the body preceding them is a real thought.

110
00:08:04,745 --> 00:08:05,511
[nm]: It's your body.

111
00:08:06,480 --> 00:08:10,829
[nm]: That is what your body is, at that level, at that time.

112
00:08:18,505 --> 00:08:23,696
[nm]: Again, you can go back to the satipaṭṭhāna, mindfulness of the bodily postures.

113
00:08:23,840 --> 00:08:24,960
[nm]: You're seated now.

114
00:08:26,710 --> 00:08:28,442
[nm]: Your body is in a certain position.

115
00:08:30,362 --> 00:08:37,229
[nm]: So, whether you look at it, whether I'm telling you about it, whether you're touching the chair, that's all because you're seated already.

116
00:08:40,442 --> 00:08:45,751
[nm]: And in a sense, that cannot... that the body is seated is a thought.

117
00:08:47,970 --> 00:08:49,667
[nm]: But then, what else would you expect it to be?

118
00:08:51,002 --> 00:08:56,088
[nm]: Because all of the sight, sound, smell, taste and touches are known because they manifest in mind.

119
00:08:56,088 --> 00:09:01,570
[nm]: I.e.: they're also thoughts that correspond to respective senses.

120
00:09:03,760 --> 00:09:06,509
[nm]: But sense in itself, without the mind, is incomprehensible.

121
00:09:10,210 --> 00:09:14,791
[nm]: So, thoughts that concern your sight are thoughts of your sight.

122
00:09:17,178 --> 00:09:19,595
[nm]: Or of your eye organ, if you want to put it like that.

123
00:09:19,650 --> 00:09:21,911
[nm]: That's why there's six different types of consciousness.

124
00:09:22,231 --> 00:09:24,905
[nm]: There's six different types of thoughts, you can say it like that.

125
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:27,852
[nm]: They're different.

126
00:09:28,703 --> 00:09:30,143
[nm]: They all appear to be looking the same.

127
00:09:30,981 --> 00:09:33,709
[nm]: But they're bound to different things, thus they're different.

128
00:09:38,130 --> 00:09:39,040
[tn]: [?It's all thoughts]

129
00:09:40,440 --> 00:09:41,604
[nm ]: Thoughts about a smell?

130
00:09:42,454 --> 00:09:46,463
[nm]: Oh, it seems just a thought about a smell, or thought about a sight.

131
00:09:47,477 --> 00:09:48,496
[nm]: Seems it's a thought.

132
00:09:48,501 --> 00:09:49,524
[nm]: And yeah, that is in common.

133
00:09:49,625 --> 00:09:50,513
[nm]: They're both thoughts.

134
00:09:50,520 --> 00:09:51,831
[nm]: They both pertain to the mind.

135
00:09:52,040 --> 00:09:53,191
[nm]: But they're different thoughts.

136
00:09:53,861 --> 00:09:54,665
[nm]: In the nature.

137
00:09:55,242 --> 00:09:57,056
[nm]: One is bound with the eye organ.

138
00:09:57,178 --> 00:09:59,090
[nm]: Another one is bound with the nose organ.

139
00:10:01,911 --> 00:10:06,606
[nm]: So, a thought of your body being there, mental, is bound with the presence of the body.

140
00:10:07,730 --> 00:10:09,018
[nm]: With the sixth sense base.

141
00:10:09,020 --> 00:10:09,987
[nm]: With the entire thing.

142
00:10:14,517 --> 00:10:15,823
[nm]: So, keeping the thought.

143
00:10:15,830 --> 00:10:17,216
[nm]: You don't even keep it, actually.

144
00:10:17,444 --> 00:10:18,096
[nm]: That's the thing.

145
00:10:18,100 --> 00:10:19,355
[nm]: That's how we develop mindfulness.

146
00:10:19,350 --> 00:10:24,846
[nm]: It's not constant keeping in your mind, because it will drive you mad eventually.

147
00:10:25,730 --> 00:10:30,449
[nm]: It's recognizing the different layers of that generality whereby things appear.

148
00:10:30,445 --> 00:10:40,921
[nm]: So, you have particular things while you're seated on the chair, what you're doing, holding something in your hand, or listening, talking, all of that while you are being seated.

149
00:10:43,474 --> 00:10:54,499
[nm]: But, see, if you forget that you were seated, and then you continue on doing things while you're seated, on one level you lost some mindfulness,

150
00:10:54,520 --> 00:11:01,923
[nm]: but the thing is, you can remember it in a mindful way that would make your memory mindful.

151
00:11:03,649 --> 00:11:23,590
[nm]: In other words, you might lose the actual awareness of your "I am seated on this chair", but if halfway through whatever you were doing, you remember, literally remember, that you are still being seated, and that is the anchor, that was the anchor of your mindfulness, that memory becomes mindful.

152
00:11:25,881 --> 00:11:30,902
[nm]: So, that which you've done in that, like, time span,

153
00:11:31,870 --> 00:11:36,060
[nm]: when you forgot, and now you remember, that also is rendered mindful.

154
00:11:36,853 --> 00:11:37,158
[nm]: Why?

155
00:11:37,150 --> 00:11:49,013
[nm]: Because the position of a body thrown in the world, random, existing on its own, given five aggregates, something you can never appropriate, actually.

156
00:11:49,756 --> 00:11:51,660
[nm]: Yet, your whole experience depends upon it.

157
00:11:54,396 --> 00:11:56,712
[nm]: And mindfulness of bodily postures revealed that.

158
00:12:00,038 --> 00:12:01,017
[nm]: Positioned body.

159
00:12:01,950 --> 00:12:06,567
[nm]: Because of which I can do, I can think, I can worry, I can be angry, I can be happy, I can be this, I can be that.

160
00:12:06,948 --> 00:12:07,977
[nm]: Because the... like...

161
00:12:08,389 --> 00:12:09,669
[nm]: I don't mean because you're seated.

162
00:12:09,660 --> 00:12:11,352
[nm]: I mean because the body is there.

163
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:21,657
[nm]: Seated, standing, walking, lying down, is just like a little extra reminder of: a body being there.

164
00:12:24,392 --> 00:12:25,649
[nm]: And that's always the...

165
00:12:26,620 --> 00:12:28,678
[nm]: Those are always the foundations of your experience.

166
00:12:28,680 --> 00:12:36,373
[nm]: No matter how great, or how lowly, or how depressed, or how late your experience might be in general, the fact is, it all requires a body to be there.

167
00:12:36,800 --> 00:12:38,740
[tn]: But I can recognize the posture, and I can...

168
00:12:38,929 --> 00:12:39,940
[tn]: [??]

169
00:12:40,171 --> 00:12:41,424
[nm]: Yeah, you recognize the posture.

170
00:12:41,489 --> 00:12:47,215
[nm]: But the thing is, you can't keep it actual in front of you all the time, because other things will start arising, because that's just how things work.

171
00:12:47,813 --> 00:12:48,613
[nm]: So, that's not the point.

172
00:12:48,613 --> 00:12:54,952
[nm]: Everybody can... like, vipassana people, when they're touching, touching, walking, walking, sitting, sitting, they're all recognizing the posture, but that's not the point.

173
00:12:55,470 --> 00:12:57,615
[nm]: The point is to recognize it and then let it go.

174
00:12:58,403 --> 00:12:59,782
[nm]: Let it go wherever it wants to go.

175
00:13:00,718 --> 00:13:05,001
[nm]: And as long as you don't stand up, you won't lose mindfulness of the fact that you're seated.

176
00:13:05,001 --> 00:13:07,112
[nm]: So, you don't actually have to be trying to be mindful.

177
00:13:07,270 --> 00:13:10,994
[nm]: You're mindful by position... by your body being positioned. So, your body is mindful.

178
00:13:12,240 --> 00:13:22,369
[nm]: Which is how that mindfulness can let... can... well, can never lapse or lapsing of that mindfulness becomes less and less occurring.

179
00:13:24,011 --> 00:13:25,809
[nm]: So, the arahant has the supreme mindfulness.

180
00:13:27,280 --> 00:13:27,561
[nm]: Why?

181
00:13:27,560 --> 00:13:32,552
[nm]: Because even when he forgets, that forgetfulness is mindful.

182
00:13:34,662 --> 00:13:36,476
[nm]: Because it's in regard to particular things.

183
00:13:37,177 --> 00:13:42,742
[nm]: But his body is situated there, in one posture or the other, and that's his mindfulness.

184
00:13:43,028 --> 00:13:47,386
[tn]: But a person has to anchor themselves back and back.

185
00:13:47,843 --> 00:13:51,916
[tn]: You know, in the beginning, it was earlier, you're seated [?pum pum pum].

186
00:13:52,540 --> 00:13:55,973
[tn]: See. And then you find yourself [?oddly], you just, you drift off.

187
00:13:55,980 --> 00:13:57,222
[nm]: You drift off, yeah, okay.

188
00:13:57,240 --> 00:13:57,740
[tn]: It's all about this.

189
00:13:57,750 --> 00:13:58,777
[nm]: But are you still seated?

190
00:13:59,440 --> 00:14:00,754
[tn]: And then I realize I'm still seated.

191
00:14:00,769 --> 00:14:01,017
[nm]: Yeah.

192
00:14:01,843 --> 00:14:07,447
[nm]: See, the problem is, with that, people keep overdoing it, because you don't know what you're supposed to achieve.

193
00:14:07,830 --> 00:14:11,051
[nm]: So, that's why I say, understanding mindfulness will make you mindful.

194
00:14:12,118 --> 00:14:16,000
[nm]: So, you're seated now, and you're mindful that you're seated, and now you drift off.

195
00:14:17,916 --> 00:14:21,249
[nm]: But if, at any point, you'll feel drifted off, I ask you,

196
00:14:22,407 --> 00:14:23,219
[nm]: Are you sitting?

197
00:14:23,432 --> 00:14:25,310
[nm]: Are you sitting or are you seated?

198
00:14:25,775 --> 00:14:26,571
[nm]: You would say yes.

199
00:14:28,537 --> 00:14:33,801
[nm]: So, the knowledge of the body position pertains to the body and it's there with the body.

200
00:14:35,375 --> 00:14:40,727
[nm]: So, that's why you can afford to forget it, in that mental keeping it in front of me all the time sense.

201
00:14:42,770 --> 00:14:43,379
[nm]: It takes time.

202
00:14:43,390 --> 00:14:50,685
[nm]: It's basically recognizing the peripheral, to the extent necessary that things don't...

203
00:14:51,752 --> 00:15:00,240
[nm]: Well, to the extent necessary that forgetting particular things doesn't induce general non-mindfulness.

204
00:15:01,020 --> 00:15:02,007
[nm]: You can put it like that.

205
00:15:06,380 --> 00:15:14,419
[nm]: So, you might have lost a particular thought that I am seated here now, but you are still seated here now.

206
00:15:15,394 --> 00:15:15,866
[nm]: Which means,

207
00:15:16,750 --> 00:15:21,619
[nm]: Even when you were thinking, I'm seated here now, that wasn't your mindfulness.

208
00:15:21,870 --> 00:15:27,466
[nm]: The fact that you were seated right there and then, that's where your mindfulness was, or could have been.

209
00:15:38,690 --> 00:15:39,912
[tn]: You see, right? If I...

210
00:15:40,714 --> 00:15:46,858
[tn]: from time to time in the day, I say, I sit down and I do something specific meditation, mindfulness of breathing.

211
00:15:48,550 --> 00:15:51,611
[tn]: I say, well, I will, I keep that in mind.

212
00:15:52,232 --> 00:15:53,460
[tn]: I'll be mindful of my breathing.

213
00:15:56,114 --> 00:15:57,961
[tn]: And I sit there for a while, but then I get up.

214
00:15:59,080 --> 00:16:00,441
[tn]: I think about this, think about that.

215
00:16:02,796 --> 00:16:05,770
[tn]: Then I might say, I'll be mindful of my body posture.

216
00:16:07,040 --> 00:16:08,704
[tn]: I'll be mindful of my feelings.

217
00:16:09,306 --> 00:16:10,308
[tn]: I'll be mindful of this.

218
00:16:10,630 --> 00:16:13,306
[tn]: But then, am I... am I?

219
00:16:13,306 --> 00:16:19,280
[tn]: I feel that I'm aware of my situation, my surroundings, the state of my mind.

220
00:16:20,685 --> 00:16:21,630
[tn]: But then I have doubt.

221
00:16:21,660 --> 00:16:22,750
[tn]: Am I actually being...

222
00:16:22,994 --> 00:16:24,170
[nm]: mindful of that particular thing?

223
00:16:24,880 --> 00:16:26,346
[tn]: Yeah. Because I've forgotten

224
00:16:26,350 --> 00:16:35,219
[nm]: Well, because you have to find your bodily posture, your breathing, your feelings, whatever you want to be mindful of.

225
00:16:35,640 --> 00:16:39,699
[nm]: You have to find that within the general situation.

226
00:16:40,095 --> 00:16:40,929
[nm]: Not in front of it.

227
00:16:44,281 --> 00:16:48,373
[nm]: So, in that general situation, that's... that's how you have to start.

228
00:16:48,824 --> 00:16:56,090
[nm]: Then, within that, without abandoning the... the image of general situation, you have to start discerning feeling.

229
00:16:56,845 --> 00:16:59,090
[nm]: You have to start discerning presence of the body.

230
00:16:59,603 --> 00:17:02,930
[tn]: In this general situation, if I, eh...

231
00:17:04,457 --> 00:17:06,182
[tn]: I... yeah, I feel like in a...

232
00:17:06,186 --> 00:17:06,582
[tn]: I can...

233
00:17:07,066 --> 00:17:08,708
[tn]: I'm aware of the general situation, but

234
00:17:11,287 --> 00:17:13,108
[tn]: I'm surrounded by it, in a way.

235
00:17:13,380 --> 00:17:13,718
[nm]: Yeah.

236
00:17:14,023 --> 00:17:14,563
[tn]: I'm within it.

237
00:17:14,647 --> 00:17:15,699
[nm]: It's [?entire], yeah

238
00:17:15,980 --> 00:17:26,163
[tn]: And whatever I think of as the body, within that, that stands for the body.

239
00:17:27,508 --> 00:17:28,022
[nm]: Pretty much.

240
00:17:28,647 --> 00:17:30,822
[tn]: And, but that can be a number of things.

241
00:17:30,970 --> 00:17:31,245
[nm]: Yeah.

242
00:17:32,060 --> 00:17:33,466
[nm]: But all [?with]... but...

243
00:17:33,920 --> 00:17:35,730
[nm]: Inseperable from a body.

244
00:17:36,998 --> 00:17:37,935
[nm]: It's conceivable.

245
00:17:38,040 --> 00:17:41,980
[tn]: It'll be a thought, but always within the general...

246
00:17:43,188 --> 00:17:46,632
[nm]: Sure, have a thought of general situation.

247
00:17:47,139 --> 00:17:50,472
[tn]: But if I do have a thought of general situation, is that not making it in front of me?

248
00:17:51,348 --> 00:17:51,965
[nm]: It depends.

249
00:17:52,499 --> 00:17:52,971
[tn]: Yes.

250
00:17:57,540 --> 00:18:00,979
[nm]: Whether it's going to be in front of you or not, it depends how you attend it.

251
00:18:01,055 --> 00:18:04,049
[nm]: If you over-attend it, under-attend it, miss-attend it.

252
00:18:04,720 --> 00:18:06,045
[nm]: If you don't attend it properly...

253
00:18:07,428 --> 00:18:08,168
[nm]: General situation.

254
00:18:08,800 --> 00:18:09,680
[nm]: Yeah, that's okay.

255
00:18:09,836 --> 00:18:10,689
[nm]: You can think behind you.

256
00:18:11,436 --> 00:18:15,410
[nm]: But then, if you over-attend "behind me", that can become in front of you.

257
00:18:16,685 --> 00:18:18,316
[tn]: Because must my mind be split?

258
00:18:19,071 --> 00:18:21,091
[nm]: Well, it doesn't really matter that much, actually.

259
00:18:21,250 --> 00:18:25,081
[nm]: What matters is to develop the sense of the mindfulness of "while".

260
00:18:26,739 --> 00:18:30,106
[nm]: The two simultaneous layers, if you want to put it that way.

261
00:18:32,733 --> 00:18:33,074
[tn]: Okay.

262
00:18:33,970 --> 00:18:35,836
[tn]: Yeah, particulars... if you [??]

263
00:18:35,840 --> 00:18:39,280
[nm]: Well, the particular is that, or the bodily and mental.

264
00:18:39,480 --> 00:18:41,089
[nm]: You can put it as crudely as that.

265
00:18:43,200 --> 00:18:49,657
[nm]: But then, obviously, both bodily and mental are mental, in a certain way.

266
00:18:50,010 --> 00:18:54,811
[nm]: But there are mental things that pertain solely to mental, and there are mental things to the bodily.

267
00:18:56,342 --> 00:19:00,041
[nm]: Thus, mental is split into bodily and mental.

268
00:19:01,690 --> 00:19:04,624
[nm]: So, in that sense, everything is... your mind comes first.

269
00:19:04,640 --> 00:19:06,236
[nm]: Just without mind, it's inconceivable.

270
00:19:06,521 --> 00:19:09,070
[nm]: But not everything is entirely mental.

271
00:19:11,424 --> 00:19:18,990
[nm]: But even the whole thing of body and mind will not be able to stand if there is no body that is conscious out there, but everywhere in the world.

272
00:19:26,491 --> 00:19:27,017
[tn]: Yees.

273
00:19:28,860 --> 00:19:33,302
[tn]: Or, as you probably says, the Pali word for situation of [?passana]

274
00:19:36,022 --> 00:19:36,430
[nm]: Vipassana.

275
00:19:37,860 --> 00:19:40,994
[nm]: Well, it's, eh... Yeah, I suppose.

276
00:19:41,135 --> 00:19:43,066
[nm]: But you have to start from the state of puttujana.

277
00:19:43,630 --> 00:19:48,735
[nm]: So, being contacted, having things manifested, that would be the original situation.

278
00:19:50,070 --> 00:19:57,737
[nm]: By recognizing the original situation, you can eventually go through it, literally, discern through it,

279
00:19:58,975 --> 00:20:00,681
[nm]: Not left, right, above, below.

280
00:20:00,680 --> 00:20:01,493
[nm]: Right through it.

281
00:20:02,087 --> 00:20:04,323
[nm]: And that's how you cease to regard it as mine.

282
00:20:05,676 --> 00:20:06,967
[nm]: So, then you're not contacted.

283
00:20:08,129 --> 00:20:09,299
[tn]: But there's still arising.

284
00:20:09,310 --> 00:20:09,634
[nm]: Yeah.

285
00:20:09,638 --> 00:20:11,878
[nm]: So, puttujana situation is contact.

286
00:20:12,650 --> 00:20:14,491
[nm]: But situation will pretend to arising.

287
00:20:15,443 --> 00:20:17,577
[nm]: Arising in passing away of the five aggregates.

288
00:20:19,958 --> 00:20:23,302
[nm]: But if that touches you, if you make it mine, then you're contacted by it.

289
00:20:23,946 --> 00:20:25,748
[nm]: If it doesn't, then you're not.

290
00:20:29,280 --> 00:20:35,733
[tn]: Then, if the situation, general situation, you said that, that's...

291
00:20:35,748 --> 00:20:38,400
[nm]: About this, before I forget it, because I forgot it once, I wanted to say...

292
00:20:40,320 --> 00:20:47,824
[nm]: You can induce the mindfulness of a general situation.

293
00:20:48,500 --> 00:20:51,615
[nm]: And while you're mindful of the general situation, let your body do things.

294
00:20:52,940 --> 00:20:54,361
[nm]: Walk, sit, move about.

295
00:20:55,459 --> 00:20:57,010
[nm]: While you're mindful of the general situation,

296
00:20:59,824 --> 00:21:10,339
[nm]: Because that indirect way of seeing that body, not directly doing it, but letting it do, while you're looking at it through the mindful general situation, is one among the bodies.

297
00:21:11,626 --> 00:21:13,516
[nm]: One among the experience of the bodies.

298
00:21:14,186 --> 00:21:15,603
[tn]: Every mindful of the body.

299
00:21:15,780 --> 00:21:16,003
[nm]: Yeah.

300
00:21:16,868 --> 00:21:18,480
[nm]: And that's the whole point of anapanasati.

301
00:21:19,040 --> 00:21:29,062
[nm]: Through doing breath, you do other things through this thing, which means they'll never be directly done,

302
00:21:29,527 --> 00:21:32,209
[nm]: They'll be indirectly observed while they're done.

303
00:21:34,914 --> 00:21:42,243
[nm]: And what you feel there, what you perceive there, what you do there, is a feeling, is a perception, is something that's well done.

304
00:21:45,447 --> 00:21:51,930
[nm]: So, you have to start recognizing that indirectly, peripherally, seeing something remotely, still stands for that thing that you're seeing remotely.

305
00:21:52,310 --> 00:21:53,641
[nm]: Not just directly in front of you.

306
00:21:54,890 --> 00:21:56,201
[nm]: That's how mindfulness develops.

307
00:21:56,472 --> 00:21:58,514
[nm]: So, while you're mindful of the entire situation,

308
00:21:59,500 --> 00:22:09,676
[nm]: your body is seated there, on its own, almost as if it has its own existence, independent of you and your general situation, so to speak, not entirely.

309
00:22:10,370 --> 00:22:14,815
[nm]: But, in a way, yes, because you don't have to be sitting to be seated.

310
00:22:15,085 --> 00:22:15,733
[nm]: You're seated.

311
00:22:16,529 --> 00:22:20,083
[nm]: But there is something the body does, yet you don't have to keep doing it.

312
00:22:20,083 --> 00:22:20,948
[nm]: Same with breathing.

313
00:22:22,087 --> 00:22:25,996
[nm]: You can be doing the breathing, but the body is also doing the breathing.

314
00:22:27,820 --> 00:22:31,481
[nm]: So you can be mindful of that breathing, as well, while you're mindful of the general situation.

315
00:22:33,017 --> 00:22:42,735
[nm]: So that... As if, like, because you're mindful of the general situation, you cannot be fully absorbed 100% into breathing or sitting or whatever else.

316
00:22:42,761 --> 00:22:43,927
[nm]: And that's the whole point.

317
00:22:44,441 --> 00:22:45,135
[nm]: To not be.

318
00:22:45,824 --> 00:22:48,857
[nm]: Because then you start recognizing it in indirect, peripherally...

319
00:22:49,640 --> 00:22:53,851
[nm]: Which is, again, the reason why this whole vipassana mainstream is completely wrong.

320
00:22:54,704 --> 00:22:55,398
[tn]: Because there's only one...

321
00:22:55,620 --> 00:23:00,514
[nm]: Well, yeah, they believe you can have a hundred percent attention upon the one thing, and you can't.

322
00:23:00,662 --> 00:23:01,725
[nm]: That's why the frustration...

323
00:23:01,721 --> 00:23:06,030
[tn]: I think I'm trying... like I said, your mind has to be split, but I'm trying to give a hundred percent to both.

324
00:23:06,327 --> 00:23:07,348
[nm]: Yeah, yeah, exactly.

325
00:23:07,350 --> 00:23:07,699
[nm]: Yeah.

326
00:23:07,830 --> 00:23:11,512
[nm]: Your mind can be split, and then you can be trying to attend that hundred percent.

327
00:23:11,512 --> 00:23:12,308
[nm]: It's impossible.

328
00:23:13,640 --> 00:23:19,913
[nm]: Because of all of the different... because of peripheral in general, and infinity on that structure, you can't have one thing.

329
00:23:21,560 --> 00:23:27,833
[nm]: Or rather, that structure is one thing, but you can't step outside of it, and then attend it as one thing.

330
00:23:27,830 --> 00:23:28,726
[nm]: It's impossible.

331
00:23:28,784 --> 00:23:33,744
[nm]: You can only see it from within, which means it will always be nāma and rūpa.

332
00:23:36,772 --> 00:23:37,910
[tn]: Let me see one more.

333
00:23:37,910 --> 00:23:47,621
[tn]: So, the general situation, being mindful, being aware of it, and particularly those body and feelings,

334
00:23:50,240 --> 00:23:58,040
[tn]: And that awareness of the mindfulness, that's within that situation.

335
00:23:58,661 --> 00:23:59,060
[nm]: Yeah.

336
00:23:59,366 --> 00:23:59,815
[tn]: As well.

337
00:23:59,926 --> 00:24:00,166
[nm]: Yeah.

338
00:24:02,698 --> 00:24:02,960
[tn]: Which is...

339
00:24:02,963 --> 00:24:10,132
[nm]: Which is why, if you do it long enough, the belief that you can be outside of that situation will fade.

340
00:24:12,009 --> 00:24:13,689
[nm]: And that belief is sakkāyadiṭṭhi.

341
00:24:15,080 --> 00:24:18,280
[nm]: Whereby your sense of self, your personality, is outside of your experience.

342
00:24:18,280 --> 00:24:19,184
[nm]: You're just assuming.

343
00:24:19,652 --> 00:24:22,270
[nm]: Failing to see that that assumption is within this experience.

344
00:24:23,818 --> 00:24:40,233
[nm]: But if you keep seeing the situation in general, the entire situation, within that, while your mindful of situation, in my body, of what you feel or whatever, partially, because you don't want to be fully absorbing what you feel, because you forget about the situation...

345
00:24:41,753 --> 00:24:46,220
[nm]: Then, it becomes apparent that, well, whatever arises within this, will be within this situation.

346
00:24:46,996 --> 00:24:51,476
[nm]: And if you do it long enough, you stop assuming that there can be anything out of the situation.

347
00:24:52,809 --> 00:24:54,480
[tn]: Because even your assumption is within.

348
00:24:54,916 --> 00:24:55,187
[nm]: Yeah.

349
00:24:55,350 --> 00:24:57,280
[tn]: Whatever it is, about it.

350
00:25:03,230 --> 00:25:10,929
[nm]: Which is how the sense of self is then recognized peripherally, ambiguously, within that situation, as a phenomenon.

351
00:25:11,250 --> 00:25:15,870
[nm]: And if it's within that situation, it cannot be the owner of that situation, it cannot be the creator, it cannot be the master.

352
00:25:17,812 --> 00:25:24,393
[nm]: So, you abandon attavāda like that, which is the belief that your self is far more superior than your whole experience.

353
00:25:30,153 --> 00:25:32,750
[tn]: Yes, you can see yours... your choice,

354
00:25:32,750 --> 00:25:35,249
[nm]: If it's manifested, it's impermanent for a very reason.

355
00:25:35,778 --> 00:25:38,292
[nm]: And now you see it manifested, means it persists.

356
00:25:49,046 --> 00:25:50,701
[nm]: So, if you're mindful of the situation...

357
00:25:51,384 --> 00:25:55,076
[nm]: I'll stop saying situation as general, because every situation is general.

358
00:25:55,707 --> 00:26:04,520
[nm]: So, if you're mindful of the situation, and then, within that mindfulness of the situation, keep a peripheral eye on what your body is doing.

359
00:26:06,700 --> 00:26:13,603
[nm]: There won't be anything left out, because whatever arises will be between the two, and that's already included in it.

360
00:26:16,707 --> 00:26:25,476
[nm]: And if you get used to that, or rather if you develop it to the insufficient extent, then you can also see that they're mutually determining each other.

361
00:26:26,249 --> 00:26:37,252
[nm]: Your entire situation would not be manifested if this random body is still not alive, sitting on the chair, breathing, being nurtured by food or whatever else.

362
00:26:39,058 --> 00:26:39,923
[nm]: And vice versa.

363
00:26:40,913 --> 00:26:46,492
[nm]: If there is no situation recognized as such, this body will not be manifested at all within.

364
00:26:50,590 --> 00:26:52,400
[tn]: Yeah, you can't imagine... the exact situation...

365
00:26:52,409 --> 00:26:53,150
[nm]: Inconceivable.

366
00:26:53,160 --> 00:26:54,747
[nm]: Yeah, yeah, inconceive...

367
00:26:54,947 --> 00:26:56,200
[nm]: And really, like, that's the thing.

368
00:26:56,980 --> 00:26:59,196
[nm]: Like, thinking that that's already the situation.

369
00:27:01,920 --> 00:27:02,310
[tn]: But...

370
00:27:05,009 --> 00:27:05,590
[tn]: But it's there.

371
00:27:10,480 --> 00:27:13,772
[tn]: When I was... in terms of the breath, when I was watching, when I was...

372
00:27:14,580 --> 00:27:20,501
[tn]: say that, attending to the breath, and I tried to attend to that, as much as I can,

373
00:27:22,353 --> 00:27:25,270
[tn]: But... but all, align

374
00:27:25,590 --> 00:27:28,233
[tn]: Becasue, I think you wrote it, in your notes on meditation.

375
00:27:28,920 --> 00:27:43,593
[tn]: You just said now, you allow the body and the feelings to arise, by themselves, so to speak, to emerge or arise by themselves, so that you don't have to conceive it.

376
00:27:45,996 --> 00:27:49,212
[tn]: So, they're no longer conceived, they just arise as they do.

377
00:27:49,500 --> 00:27:55,052
[nm]: You recognize they would arise with whether you conceive them or not, which means my conceiving becomes redundant.

378
00:27:56,652 --> 00:28:04,049
[tn]: See, if I'm looking at the... if I'm doing anapanasati, like that, or breathing, breathing, breathing, and I'm...

379
00:28:05,390 --> 00:28:06,815
[tn]: now, I'm looking at the body.

380
00:28:08,744 --> 00:28:13,210
[tn]: Because the body arises and I'm like, oh, [?that looks like this body], which I'm not supposed to conceive.

381
00:28:15,520 --> 00:28:20,966
[nm]: Well, again, you don't conceive it necessarily just by thinking that.

382
00:28:22,910 --> 00:28:26,630
[nm]: Because, as I said, well, if you do anapanasati,

383
00:28:27,861 --> 00:28:30,160
[nm]: mindfulness of breathing is your situation.

384
00:28:30,740 --> 00:28:31,756
[nm]: I'm breathing.

385
00:28:32,612 --> 00:28:33,590
[nm]: That's your situation.

386
00:28:34,190 --> 00:28:38,175
[nm]: Within that, I'm breathing while the body is like this.

387
00:28:38,172 --> 00:28:40,215
[nm]: I'm breathing while the body is like that.

388
00:28:40,221 --> 00:28:42,513
[nm]: I'm going to breathe in while the body will be like this.

389
00:28:42,510 --> 00:28:43,381
[nm]: I'm going to breathe...

390
00:28:43,381 --> 00:28:44,892
[nm]: I'm going to breathe feeling this.

391
00:28:44,892 --> 00:28:46,243
[nm]: I'm going to breathe feeling that.

392
00:28:46,667 --> 00:28:47,461
[nm]: That's the whole point.

393
00:28:48,858 --> 00:29:00,464
[nm]: So, if you start thinking about the feeling and everything, dududududu, you can afford that, if your mindfulness gets developed to such an extent whereby an act of breathing, whether you do it or not, is where it's anchored.

394
00:29:01,492 --> 00:29:02,593
[nm]: And you are still breathing.

395
00:29:04,575 --> 00:29:11,147
[nm]: So, then, when you go back to the breathing, you go back as if it was always there, because it was always there.

396
00:29:12,083 --> 00:29:17,833
[nm]: So, your forgetting becomes mindf... well, rather, your forgetting becomes within the mindfulness.

397
00:29:19,636 --> 00:29:23,313
[nm]: So, when you remember, everything is rendered as mindful memory.

398
00:29:26,252 --> 00:29:30,190
[nm]: Mindful memory means a memory that will not induce avijja.

399
00:29:39,750 --> 00:29:42,212
[tn]: What do you mean, not induce it, not eh...

400
00:29:42,680 --> 00:29:48,723
[nm]: Well, like, an arahant can remember stuff he'd done when he was a puthujjana.

401
00:29:50,060 --> 00:29:53,673
[nm]: But none of those memories will induce a [?regeneration].

402
00:29:59,490 --> 00:30:13,732
[nm]: So, when you forget about the breathing, but then you become mindful of the fact... well, when your body is mindful, but the breathing is still happening, even if you go and think about other things, when you get back to...

403
00:30:14,212 --> 00:30:15,566
[nm]: Or rather, let's put it like this.

404
00:30:15,916 --> 00:30:26,464
[nm]: Remembering that you were supposed to be breathing, practicing mindfulness of breathing, that act won't be like, oh, I remember something I forgot.

405
00:30:27,150 --> 00:30:35,298
[nm]: Remembering will just mean bringing you back to the breathing that is already there, and was already there, and was happening all this time.

406
00:30:35,770 --> 00:30:40,633
[nm]: Thus, your mindfulness was already there, was already there, and was happening all this time.

407
00:30:42,424 --> 00:30:50,083
[nm]: So, remembering and forgetting doesn't induce avijja anymore in regard to where was I, what was I doing, how to start again.

408
00:30:51,258 --> 00:30:55,203
[nm]: It just means going somewhere else and coming back to the other thing.

409
00:30:57,440 --> 00:30:58,676
[nm]: Which is what you do all the time.

410
00:30:59,169 --> 00:31:00,018
[nm]: But you don't know that.

411
00:31:01,070 --> 00:31:02,904
[nm]: So, when you go somewhere else, you forget.

412
00:31:04,766 --> 00:31:05,261
[nm]: i.e.:

413
00:31:05,468 --> 00:31:10,632
[nm]: the assumptions of avijja and everything else, the upadāna, arise... they perpetuate.

414
00:31:26,200 --> 00:31:35,080
[tn]: You can also start from.... death, breathing, looking at the situation inside.

415
00:31:35,089 --> 00:31:35,803
[nm]: Satipaṭṭhāna. 

416
00:31:36,021 --> 00:31:36,901
[nm]: Just take any of it.

417
00:31:38,378 --> 00:31:39,400
[nm]: You can start with any of it.

418
00:31:40,160 --> 00:31:41,206
[tn]: Either the body's here...

419
00:31:42,052 --> 00:31:45,243
[nm]: But the body, but there's so many different types of practicing body mindfulness.

420
